    "killington": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Killington",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-19 16:29:01",
      "note": "Good evening, Beast fans, It was a wild weekend here at Killington and we had a blast through sunny skies or rain. A few lingering snow showers early will taper off by mid-morning tomorrow, giving way to some breaks of sun as the day rolls on. Temps stay just below 30 with a steady west wind, and only a dusting of fresh snow to start the day. Surface conditions were firmer today than as of recent as colder temps did their thing, although Skyelark and Bittersweet held much softer snow than expected and was quite the enjoyable ride, all things considered. Conditions should stay on the firmer side as it stays cool, consisting of wet granular and machine groomed hardpack. Our grooming crew will be smoothing out Superstar, Skyelark, and Bittersweet. Check the Terrain Parks Report for the full details on what we have available. Today was the last day to hit the Timberline terrain park over at Ramshead, as that area will be wrapping up operations for the season. Don’t worry though, our kparks crew will be putting in a handful of features on Skyehawk tonight for your late season rail jamming needs. The Superstar Six is scheduled to spin starting at 9:00 a.m. Please note that there is no longer any beginner terrain available. Have a great week! - Evan Operating Day: 159 Season passes for 26/27 are now on sale! Lock in the lowest price on Beast 365 or Winter Unlimited passes with lots of perks, plus free skiing & riding for the rest of this spring. And there's more good news for families: Youth & Child pass pricing has been significantly reduced for next season, with over $300 in savings available on Beast 365 access. Lifts The Superstar Six will operate seven days a week from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Monday through Friday, from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. on Saturday, and from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Sunday. Starting on May 3rd, the Superstar Six will be open Friday through Sunday while conditions allow. The Tubing Park presented by bubly is closed for the season. Uphill Travel Uphill travel is now closed for this season. Please visit killington.com/uphill for full information on our uphill travel policies. MOUNTAIN SERVICES Parking & Shuttles Parking is available at our K-1 Lodge and at the top of Killington Road. Vale Road is closed Monday - Friday for road work and on Saturday mornings to facilitate Snowdon Triple chair pickups. Please respect signage and allow our parking staff to assist you on your trip to the slopes. Shuttle service is available from 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. midweek and 6:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends and holidays through Sunday, May 3rd unless otherwise stated in this report. Winter car camping and overnight parking is only available in the lot across from Skyeship Lodge, though please note that the Skyeship Lodge is closed for this season. See details here . Lodge Services All lodges listed here are open daily from 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekdays and 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends/peak dates*. K-1 Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served from 10:30 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. daily with limited offerings midweek. Brew Bar (2nd floor): Open serving handcrafted coffees, cocktails, and beers starting at 9:00 a.m. daily. K-1 Pub (3rd floor): Closed for the season. Rentals & Killington Sports at K-1: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Demos & Tuning: Available via the K-1 Rental Shop from April 10th through May 3rd. All pass holders—including Beast 365 and Unlimited—will receive 50% off demo rentals. Guest Services: 1st floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 1:00 p.m. on weekdays and until 4:30 p.m. on weekends/peak dates. 2nd floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Superstar Umbrella Bar: Open at 11:00 a.m. from Friday - Sunday offering beer, wine, liquor, and specialty hot cocktails. Ramshead Lodge - Closed for the season. Bear Mountain Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Demos & Tuning remains open seven days a week, providing tuning services for guests and Season Tune holders. Demos also available with more options at K-1. Skyeship Lodge - Closed for the season. On-Mountain Dining Options : Peak Lodge – Closed for the season. Jerk Jamaican Mountain Grill – Closed for the season. Ledgewood Yurt – Closed for the season. Mountain services are subject to change. Please check here daily before making your lunch and lodge choices. Winter Lift Tickets and rentals must be purchased online at this link . Check to see if your pass is good to go using our Online Pass Checker . Find our Season Pass FAQs by clicking here . Season passes for summer 2026 and winter 26/27 are now on sale! Buy now . Have a ticketing question? Our text number ( 802-523-2202 ) is the best way to get it answered quickly, but please note that we cannot process transactions via text. Have a season pass question? Call 1-800-621-MTNS or email seasonpass@killington.com Please visit Killington.com/cancellation for more details on our cancellation policy. Killington is a cashless resort. We accept all major credit cards as well as Apple, Google, and Samsung Pay. *No remaining Peak Dates during winter 2025/26. We strive to have the most up-to-date and accurate snow report, but errors can happen from time to time. If you have feedback or a correction for us, please share it here.",
